{"title":"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_by_MathTalks\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by MathTalks</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alice needs to replace a light bulb located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters below the ceiling in her kitchen. The ceiling is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c37f385505bac74c82c67d72ae9a9f4da67e32d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> meters above the floor. Alice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> meters tall and can reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abef9fdb0235b2ede2639538b5bd76711e058fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> centimeters above the top of her head. Standing on a stool, she can just reach the light bulb. What is the height of the stool, in centimeters?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f59e62ddce8563008c163b01b93bc6ffe9e0cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 32 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 34\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 36\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 38\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Convert everything to the same unit. Since the answer is in centimeters, change meters to centimeters by moving the decimal place two places to the right.\n</p><p>The ceiling is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd7f90b1c0d050ea71e884260078e17d6ffadfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> centimeters above the floor. The combined height of Alice and the light bulb when she reaches for it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245c8d15b812069710ab1b3a21bcf06549c1b147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+150+46=206$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"159\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters. That means the stool's height needs to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b467567fa5414730a9bbd703aec9bffbf8ff95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240-206=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"165\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Convert everything to the same unit. Since the answer is in centimeters, change meters to centimeters by multiplying by 100. \n</p><p>So, the ceiling is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd7f90b1c0d050ea71e884260078e17d6ffadfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> centimeters above the floor. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm below means the light is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf4af8067704e46fb6ff3c35882ab1f2c25e3fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$230$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> cm. Because Alice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e10e5f3aa7c766cb27c3ad319fa526f71588cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> cm, and she can reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abef9fdb0235b2ede2639538b5bd76711e058fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cm <b> above her head </b>, her reach height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1e76a98ec2a5c126fb573a556c7442bb7f5c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46+150=196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />. The height of the stool is the difference of the heights; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9d7de22224b560daf2f2f9c75b0393254a5782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$230-196=34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" /> cm.\n</p><p>-N.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_by_MathTalks\">Video by MathTalks</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video by MathTalks\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/EEbksvfujhk\">https://youtu.be/EEbksvfujhk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ASeDKYPTR-Y\">https://youtu.be/ASeDKYPTR-Y</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\"